Operational runbook basics
- Observability: add request logging, latency histograms, and health endpoints (already included).
- Capacity: monitor heap usage; if XML grows beyond safe memory, switch USE_MONGO=true.
- Reload: POST /api/lookup/reload with header x-admin-token while in-memory mode.
- Indexes: in Mongo mode, ensure indexes via a one-time job or at app start using ensureMongoIndexes with the injected model.

Rollout checklist
- Build image and run locally with docker-compose (in-memory), verify endpoints.
- Seed Mongo using tools/xml_to_mongo.ts; run in Mongo mode and verify parity.
- Deploy to staging on Kubernetes; run shadow tests comparing responses vs .NET.
- Enable canary (5–10% traffic) using your ingress or service mesh; monitor SLOs.
- Promote to 100%; keep feature flag for quick rollback (toggle USE_MONGO or revert image).

